134 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 116 0 R
/T (Ransomware is a growing cybersecurity threat that can make important files unavailable by rapidly changing, renaming, deleting, or encrypting them. In many cases, traditional security tools detect the attack only after several files have already been affected. This makes early detection important, especially when file activity suddenly increases within a short period.)
/E (Ransomware is a growing cybersecurity threat that can make important files unavailable by rapidly changing, renaming, deleting, or encrypting them. In many cases, traditional security tools detect the attack only after several files have already been affected. This makes early detection important, especially when file activity suddenly increases within a short period.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
135 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 116 0 R
/T (This project proposes a lightweight Android early-warning system that detects ransomware-like file activity in a controlled lab environment. The system monitors a designated test folder on an Android emulator or rooted lab device and looks for unusual behavior, such as many files being modified quickly, repeated file renaming, extension changes, file replacement, or deletion of original files.)
/E (This project proposes a lightweight Android early-warning system that detects ransomware-like file activity in a controlled lab environment. The system monitors a designated test folder on an Android emulator or rooted lab device and looks for unusual behavior, such as many files being modified quickly, repeated file renaming, extension changes, file replacement, or deletion of original files.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
136 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 116 0 R
/T (Instead of relying on malware signatures, the prototype uses behavior-based rules and a sliding time window to identify suspicious patterns. It also considers normal activities, such as editing documents, copying files, backups, or synchronization, to reduce false alerts. When suspicious activity crosses a defined threshold, the system immediately generates an alert and stops only the registered simulated attack process.)
/E (Instead of relying on malware signatures, the prototype uses behavior-based rules and a sliding time window to identify suspicious patterns. It also considers normal activities, such as editing documents, copying files, backups, or synchronization, to reduce false alerts. When suspicious activity crosses a defined threshold, the system immediately generates an alert and stops only the registered simulated attack process.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
137 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 116 0 R
/T (The project uses synthetic files and harmless ransomware-like simulations only. It does not use real ransomware, access files from other applications, or claim to provide device-wide protection on stock Android devices. The performance of the prototype will be measured using detection delay, number of files affected before alert, precision, recall, and false-positive rate.)
/E (The project uses synthetic files and harmless ransomware-like simulations only. It does not use real ransomware, access files from other applications, or claim to provide device-wide protection on stock Android devices. The performance of the prototype will be measured using detection delay, number of files affected before alert, precision, recall, and false-positive rate.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
138 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 116 0 R
/T (The expected result is a simple, safe, and explainable prototype that demonstrates how early behavior-based monitoring can help identify ransomware-like activity before extensive file damage occurs.)
/E (The expected result is a simple, safe, and explainable prototype that demonstrates how early behavior-based monitoring can help identify ransomware-like activity before extensive file damage occurs.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
