684 0 obj
<<
/Title (This project proposes a lightweight Android early-warning system that detects ransomware-like file activity in a controlled lab environment. The system monitors a designated test folder on an Android emulator or rooted lab device and looks for unusual behavior, such as many files being modified quickly, repeated file renaming, extension changes, file replacement, or deletion of original files.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 364 0 R
/Prev 581 0 R
/Next 758 0 R
>>
endobj
685 0 obj
<<
/Title (The project uses synthetic files and harmless ransomware-like simulations only. It does not use real ransomware, access files from other applications, or claim to provide device-wide protection on stock Android devices. The performance of the prototype will be measured using detection delay, number of files affected before alert, precision, recall, and false-positive rate.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 364 0 R
/Prev 758 0 R
/Next 582 0 R
>>
endobj
