758 0 obj
<<
/Title (Instead of relying on malware signatures, the prototype uses behavior-based rules and a sliding time window to identify suspicious patterns. It also considers normal activities, such as editing documents, copying files, backups, or synchronization, to reduce false alerts. When suspicious activity crosses a defined threshold, the system immediately generates an alert and stops only the registered simulated attack process.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 364 0 R
/Prev 684 0 R
/Next 685 0 R
>>
endobj
759 0 obj
<<
/Title (Traditional security approaches may rely on known malware signatures or detect threats after suspicious activity has already occurred. A behavior-based approach can instead monitor file operations and identify unusual patterns that may indicate ransomware.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 583 0 R
/Prev 688 0 R
/Next 832 0 R
>>
endobj
760 0 obj
<<
/Title (The prototype will be evaluated in a controlled Android emulator using both normal workloads and simulated ransomware attacks. Performance will be measured using detection delay, precision, recall, and the number of files affected before detection.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 583 0 R
/Prev 832 0 R
/First 833 0 R
/Last 833 0 R
/Count -1
/Next 689 0 R
>>
endobj
